          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#in_singular_homology In singular homology
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \hookrightarrow X
            a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subspace"} subspace
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_\bullet(X)
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+homology"} singular homology
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_\bullet(A) \hookrightarrow C_\bullet(X)
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+map"} chain map
            induced by the subspace inclusion.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cokernel"} cokernel
              of this inclusion, hence the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_\bullet(X)/C_\bullet(A)
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_\bullet(X)
              by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_\bullet(A)
              under the inclusion, is the
              = succeed "." do
                %strong
                  chain complex of
                  = succeed "-relative" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  A
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary"} boundary
                  in this quotient is called an
                  = succeed "," do
                    %strong
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi A
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                      \-relative singular boundary
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cycle"} cycle
                  is called an
                  = succeed "." do
                    %strong
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi A
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                      \-relative singular cycle
              %li
                %p
                  The
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+homology"} chain homology
                  of the quotient is the
                  %strong
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                    \-relative singular homology of
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi H
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≔
                        %msub
                          %mi H
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        H_n(X , A)\coloneqq H_n(C_\bullet(X)/C_\bullet(A))
                        \\,.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              This means that a singular
              = succeed "-chain" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n+1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \in C_{n+1}(X)
              is an
              = succeed "-relative" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary"} boundary
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi c
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial c \in C_{n}(X)
              is, while not necessarily 0, contained in the
              = succeed "-chains" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi c
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ↪
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial c \in C_n(A) \hookrightarrow C_n(X)
              = succeed "\u201D." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#LongExactSequences Long exact sequences
          #RelativeHomologyLongExactSequence.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Let
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mover
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi i
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \stackrel{i}{\hookrightarrow} X
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/long+exact+sequence"} long exact sequence
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi H
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi δ
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi H
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\cdots
                    \\to
                    H_n(A)
                    \\stackrel{H_n(i)}{\to}
                    H_n(X)
                    \\to
                    H_n(X, A)
                    \\stackrel{\delta_{n-1}}{\to}
                    H_{n-1}(A)
                    \\stackrel{H_{n-1}(i)}{\to}
                    H_{n-1}(X)
                    \\to
                    H_{n-1}(X, A)
                    \\to
                    \\cdots
                    \\,.
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connecting+homomorphism"} connecting homomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi δ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta_{n} \colon H_{n+1}(X, A) \to H_n(A)
              sends an element
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [c] \in H_{n+1}(X, A)
              represented by an
              = succeed "-relative" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo +
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \in C_{n+1}(X)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary"} boundary
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mo ∂
                        %mi X
                      %mi c
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ↪
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial^X c \in C_n(A) \hookrightarrow C_n(X)
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              This is the
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homology+long+exact+sequence"} homology long exact sequence
              induced by the given
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/short+exact+sequence"} short exact sequence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi coker
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \to C_\bullet(A) \stackrel{i}{\hookrightarrow} C_\bullet(X) \to coker(i)  \simeq C_\bullet(X)/C_\bullet(A)  \to 0
              of chain complexes.
          #RelativeTripleHomologyLongExactSequence.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi A
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \hookrightarrow A \hookrightarrow X
              be a sequence of two inclusions. Then there is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/long+exact+sequence"} long exact sequence
              of relative homology groups of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\cdots \to H_n(A , B) \to H_n(X , B) \to H_n(X , A ) \to H_{n-1}(A , B) \to \cdots
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              Observe that we have a (degreewise)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/short+exact+sequence"} short exact sequence
              of chain complexes
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mn 0
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    0 \to C_\bullet(A)/C_\bullet(B) \to C_\bullet(X)/C_\bullet(B) \to C_\bullet(X)/C_\bullet(A) \to 0
                    \\,.
            %p
              The corresponding
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homology+long+exact+sequence"} homology long exact sequence
              is the long exact sequence in question.
          %h3#Excision Excision
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Z
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi A
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z \hookrightarrow A \hookrightarrow X
            be a sequence of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+subspace"} topological subspace
            inclusions such that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closure"} closure
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar Z
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z
            is still contained in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interior"} interior
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∘
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^\circ
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi Z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mo ↪
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mo ∘
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar Z \hookrightarrow A^\circ
          #ExcisionA.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              In the above situation, the inclusion
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo −
                    %mi Z
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo −
                    %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X-Z, A-Z) \hookrightarrow (X,A)
              induces
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              in relative singular homology groups
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo −
                    %mi Z
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo −
                    %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H_n(X-Z, A-Z) \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} H_n(X,A)
            %p
              for all
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A,B \hookrightarrow X
            be two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+subspaces"} topological subspaces
            such that their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interior"} interior
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cover"} cover
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∘
                  %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                  %msup
                    %mi B
                    %mo ∘
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^\circ \coprod B^\circ \to X
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          #ExcisionB.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              In the above situation, the inclusion
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (B, A \cap B) \hookrightarrow (X,A)
              induces
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphisms"} isomorphisms
              in relative singular homology groups
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H_n(B, A \cap B) \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} H_n(X,A)
            %p
              for all
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
          %p
            A proof is spelled out in (
            %a{:href => "#Hatcher"}> Hatcher, from p. 128 on
            ).
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              These two propositions are equivalent to each other. To see this identify
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                      %mo =
                      %mi X
                      %mo −
                      %mi Z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B = X - Z
          %h3#HomotopyInvariance Homotopy invariance
          #HomotopyInvariance.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p Relative homology is homotopy invariant in both arguments.
          %p (…)
          %h3#RelationToQuotientTopologicalSpaces Relation to reduced homology of quotient topological spaces
          #GoodPair.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+subspace"} topological subspace
              inclusion
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \hookrightarrow X
              is called a
              %strong good pair
              if
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                  is
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+subset"} closed
                  inside
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                  has an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/neighbourhood"} neighbourhood
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  which is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deformation+retract"} deformation retract
                  of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          .num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW+complex"} CW complex
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \hookrightarrow X
              is a good pair (called a
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-pair"} CW-pair
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,A)
          %p
            This is discussed at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "CW+complex#Subcomplexes"} CW complex – Subcomplexes
          #HomologyOfQuotientSpace.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_5 Proposition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \hookrightarrow X
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+subspace"} topological subspace
              inclusion which is
              %em good
              in the sense of def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GoodPair"}
              = succeed "-relative" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              coincides with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduced+singular+homology"} reduced singular homology
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+space"} quotient space
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X/A
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi H
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H_n(X , A)
                    \\simeq
                    \\tilde H_n(X/A)
                    \\,.
          %p
            For instance (
            %a{:href => "#Hatcher"}> Hatcher, prop. 2.22
            ).
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              By assumption we can find a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/neighbourhood"} neighbourhood
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi j
                    %mi U
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \stackrel{j}{\to} U \hookrightarrow X
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \hookrightarrow U
              has a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deformation+retract"} deformation retract
              and hence in particular is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalence"} homotopy equivalence
              and so induces also isomorphisms on all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+homology"} singular homology
              groups.
            %p
              It follows in particular that for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              the canonical morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi H
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi id
                        %mo ,
                        %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_n(X,A) \stackrel{H_n(id,j)}{\to} H_n(X,U)
              is an
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HomotopyInvariance"}
            %p
              Given such
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              we have an evident
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commuting diagram
              of pairs of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi id
                                %mo ,
                                %mi j
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ←
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo −
                            %mi A
                            %mo ,
                            %mi U
                            %mo −
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mo ≃
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi A
                            %mo ,
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi id
                                %mo ,
                                %mi j
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                                %mi A
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi A
                            %mo ,
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ←
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi A
                            %mo −
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi A
                            %mo ,
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi A
                            %mo −
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    (X,A) &amp;\stackrel{(id,j)}{\to}&amp; (X,U) &amp;\leftarrow&amp; (X-A, U - A)
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\simeq}}
                    \\\
                    (X/A, A/A) &amp;\stackrel{(id,j/A)}{\to}&amp; (X/A, U/A) &amp;\leftarrow&amp; (X/A - A/A, U/A - A/A)
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              Here the right vertical morphism is in fact a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphism
            %p
              Applying relative singular homology to this diagram yields for each
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commuting diagram
              of abelian groups
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi H
                              %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %munderover
                              %mo →
                              %mo ≃
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi H
                                  %mi n
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi id
                                %mo ,
                                %mi j
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi H
                              %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ←
                              %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi H
                              %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo −
                            %mi A
                            %mo ,
                            %mi U
                            %mo −
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mo ≃
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi H
                              %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi A
                            %mo ,
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %munderover
                              %mo →
                              %mo ≃
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi H
                                  %mi n
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi id
                                %mo ,
                                %mi j
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                                %mi A
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi H
                              %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi A
                            %mo ,
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ←
                              %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi H
                              %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi A
                            %mo −
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi A
                            %mo ,
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi A
                            %mo −
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    H_n(X,A) &amp;\underoverset{\simeq}{H_n(id,j)}{\to}&amp; H_n(X,U) &amp;\stackrel{\simeq}{\leftarrow}&amp; H_n(X-A, U - A)
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\simeq}}
                    \\\
                    H_n(X/A, A/A) &amp;\underoverset{\simeq}{H_n(id,j/A)}{\to}&amp; H_n(X/A, U/A) &amp;\stackrel{\simeq}{\leftarrow}&amp; H_n(X/A - A/A, U/A - A/A)
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              Here the left horizontal morphisms are the above isomorphims induced from the deformation retract. The right horizontal morphisms are isomorphisms by prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ExcisionA"}
              and the right vertical morphism is an isomorphism since it is induced by a homeomorphism. Hence the left vertical morphism is an isomorphism (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-out-of-3"} 2-out-of-3
              for isomorphisms).
          %h3#RelationToReducedHomology Relation to reduced homology
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_6 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+set"} inhabited
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mo *
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \colon  * \hookrightarrow X
              any point. Then the relative singular homology
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_n(X , *)
              is isomorphic to the absolute
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduced+singular+homology"} reduced singular homology
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi H
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde H_n(X)
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi H
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H_n(X , *) \simeq \tilde H_n(X)
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_4 Proof
            %p
              This is the special case of prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HomologyOfQuotientSpace"}
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              a point.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#basic_examples Basic examples
          .num_example
            %h6#example_2 Example
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduced+singular+homology"} reduced singular homology
              of the
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere"} sphere
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^{n}
              equals the
              = succeed "-relative" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^{n-1}
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disk"} disk
              with respect to the canonical
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary"} boundary
              inclusion
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo ↪
                      %msup
                        %mi D
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^{n-1} \hookrightarrow D^n
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi H
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi D
                      %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\tilde H_\bullet(S^n) \simeq H_\bullet(D^n, S^{n-1})
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_5 Proof
            %p
              The
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere"} sphere
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphic
              to the
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disk"} disk
              with its entire
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary"} boundary
              identified with a point:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi n
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi D
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    S^n \simeq D^n/S^{n-1}
                    \\,.
            %p
              Moreover the boundary inclusion is evidently a
              %em good pair
              in the sense of def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GoodPair"}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HomologyOfQuotientSpace"}
          %h3#detecting_homology_isomorphisms Detecting homology isomorphisms
          .num_example
            %h6#example_3 Example
            %p
              If an inclusion
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \hookrightarrow X
              is such that all relative homology vanishes,
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi H
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_\bullet(X , A) \simeq 0
          .proof
            %h6#proof_6 Proof
            %p
              Under the given assumotion the long exact sequence in prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RelativeHomologyLongExactSequence"}
              secomposes into short exact pieces of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mn 0
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    0 \to H_n(A) \to H_n(X) \to 0
                    \\,.
            %p
              Exactness says that the middle morphism here is an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
          %h3#RelativeHomologyOfCWComplexes Relative homology of CW-complexes
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-complex"} CW-complex
            and write
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 0
                  %mo ↪
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ↪
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  X_0 \hookrightarrow X_1 \hookrightarrow X_2 \hookrightarrow \cdots \hookrightarrow X
          %p
            for its
            = succeed "-structure" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+topological+space"} filtered topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{n+1}
            the topological space obtained from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_n
            by gluing on
            = succeed "-cells." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n+1)
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_7 Proposition
            %p The relative singular homology of the filtering degrees is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi k
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi ℤ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                              %mi Cells
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi X
                              %msub
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mi n
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mtd
                              %mi if
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mi k
                              %mo =
                              %mi n
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mn 0
                            %mtd
                              %mi otherwise
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H_n(X_k , X_{k-1})
                    \\simeq
                    \\left\{
                    \\array{
                    \\mathbb{Z}[Cells(X)_n] &amp; if\; k = n
                    \\\
                    0 &amp; otherwise
                    }
                    \\right.
                    \\,,
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cells
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cells(X)_n \in Set
              denotes the set of
              = succeed "-cells" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi Cells
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}[Cells(X)_n]
              denotes the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+abelian+group"} free abelian group
              on this set.
          %p
            For instance (
            %a{:href => "#Hatcher"}> Hatcher, lemma 2.34
            ).
          .proof
            %h6#proof_7 Proof
            %p
              The inclusion
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ↪
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{k-1} \hookrightarrow X_k
              is clearly a
              %em good pair
              in the sense of def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GoodPair"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_k/X_{k-1}
              is by definition of CW-complexes a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wedge+sum"} wedge sum
              of
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spheres"} spheres
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi kCell
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} kCell
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HomologyOfQuotientSpace"}
              we have an isomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi k
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi H
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_n(X_k , X_{k-1}) \simeq \tilde H_n( X_k / X_{k-1})
              with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduced+homology"} reduced homology
              of this wedge sum. The statement then follows by the respect of reduced homology for wedge sums as discussed at
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "reduced+homology#RelationToWedgeSums"} Reduced homology - Respect for wedge sums
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+cohomology"} relative cohomology
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cellular+homology"} cellular homology
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gauss-Manin+connection"} Gauss-Manin connection
          %h2#references References
          %p A standard textbook account for relative singular homology is section 2.1 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Allen+Hatcher"}> Allen Hatcher
              ,
              %em
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.cornell.edu/~hatcher/AT/ATpage.html"} Algebraic Topology
